course: dictionary
lesson: 293
title: Amusement: funny feelings and fun places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amusement is a noun, and it has more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find the right one. «Where's the amusement in that?» asks where the funny part is, so here amusement means the feeling of finding something funny.
explain: Context often shows the meaning. «The clown tripped over, much to my amusement.» The phrase much to my amusement tells you the speaker found it funny. If you watch something in amusement, you watch it and enjoy it because it makes you laugh.
explain: Plural amusements can mean rides and games. «We walked along the seaside amusements.» Seaside and rides are the clues here, so amusements means the fair-like places by the sea. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have probably found it.
fact: Amusement means the feeling of finding something funny.
fact: Amusement can also mean fun or entertainment, something that keeps you entertained.
fact: The plural amusements means rides and games at a fair or seaside.
fact: Useful phrases: amusement park, amusement arcade, for amusement, much to my amusement.
fact: «Silly boyish amusement» describes a playful, giggly kind of feeling about something silly.
exercise: «Where's the amusement in that?» What does amusement mean here? | *Where is the funny or fun part of that? | Where is the cake? | Where is the nearest exit? | Where is the money kept?
exercise: «Silly boyish amusement.» What kind of feeling is this? | Being scared of the dark | Being cross about a broken toy | *Being amused, finding something funny | Being tired after a long day
exercise: Ella and Sam spent the afternoon on the seaside amusements, riding and playing games. What are the amusements? | *Rides and games at a fair or seaside | Lessons in a classroom | Long walks along the cliffs | Sandcastles on the beach
test: «The clown tripped over, much to my amusement.» What does amusement mean? | Fear | *Finding it funny | Boredom | Sadness
test: An amusement arcade is a place with games machines. What is it? | *A room of games machines for fun | A museum of old paintings | A bank for saving money | A shop selling shoes
exam: Which phrase means a place with rides and games? | *Amusement park | Hospital | Museum | Library
